 "A screen camera with command buffers draws into a texture standing for the screen (Unbound's, an sRGB RGBA8 render texture, format 71: a Blit from its CameraTarget reads the camera's image, tests/projects/rtdepth); the macOS Editor's callback in that camera's command buffer finds the screen's own BGRA8Unorm color texture (80). Its size, depth and actions match": [
  "plugin.state.color0.screencamera"
 ],
 "A Blit from a screen camera's target: green 0x36 against the Editor's 0x37. The batch-mode Editor's screen is BGRA8Unorm without sRGB encoding and keeps the camera's linear 0.214 as 0x37; Unbound's stand-in is sRGB-encoded, where that value (encoded 127.5) is stored as 127 on Metal, presumably a tie (as the Editor's Metal device stores it, srgb.drawn.bytes). The windowed Editor's Game view is sRGB (BGRA8Unorm_sRGB) and reads 0x7f here (metal-windowed.jsonl)": [
  "screencamera.drawn.pixels"
 ],
 "ETC2_RGBA1, signed EAC and PVRTC layered textures: the macOS Editor keeps their blocks (8 or 32 bytes for a 4x4 level); Unbound has no decoder or renderer format of them (Texture2D neither) and keeps RGBA32 texels, warned (64 bytes). Queued": [
  "array.make.EAC_R_SIGNED",
  "array.make.ETC2_RGBA1",
  "array.make.PVRTC_RGB2",
  "array.make.PVRTC_RGBA4"
 ],
 "A dynamically scaled render texture's content after a change of scale: the macOS Editor's still holds the color it was cleared to at the old scale (uniform, so whether it is stretched or kept in place is not measured); Unbound remakes the texture at the new size, cleared. Queued": [
  "dynres.reset.texels"
 ],
